  44: 
  45: ### The three unverified reads â€” confirmed first-hand, not taken on trust
  46: 
  47: `loop/items/AI4DEV-24/plan.md:812-814` records the surviving Gate 2 finding: this item "must name
  48: all three unverified reads â€” `OpenWorld.sut`, `OpenWorld.w` and `h.fixtures.world` â€” not only the
  49: `Sut` axis", and that "the `h.fixtures` half is already closed here as a by-product, since `h` no
  50: longer carries the suite's `W`." I checked each against the current tree:
  51: 
  52: | read | status now | evidence |
  53: |---|---|---|
  54: | `OpenWorld.sut` | **OPEN** | `registry.ts:176` types `h: AtHarness` concretely, so `h.sut[key]` is `unknown`; line 544 relabels it `Sut` |
  55: | `OpenWorld.w` | **OPEN** | `w` is really `WorldSeam`; line 544 relabels it `W` |
  56: | `h.fixtures.world` | **CLOSED** | `contracts.ts:167` + `registry.ts:176`: `h` is unparameterized `AtHarness`, so `h.fixtures` is `Fixtures<WorldSeam>` and reading through `h` yields `WorldSeam`, never the suite's `W` |
  57: 
